.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::VSetConverter\fP< dim >::ConvertLinearToBarycentricTetrahedra (\fBVSet\fP< dim > & vset)"

.PP
turn linear tetrahedral mesh into 11-noded barycentric tetrahedral mesh void \fBVSetConverter<dim>::ConvertLinearToBarycentricTetrahedra( VSet<dim>& vset )\fP

.PP

.br
 \fBDescription\fP 

.PP
\fBConvertLinearToBarycentricTetrahedra()\fP transforms a 'plist' with linear tetrahedral elements into a corresponding Vdata for 11-noded barycentric tetrahedral elements numbered as follows\&.

.PP
^ t | / s | 9 / 3 o -- o --- o 2 | \\ / | | \\ / | 7 o 6 o \\ o 5 | / 8 o | | / | 0 o -- o --- o 1 ----> r 4 
.br

.PP
The center node of the barycentric tetrahedron has the number 10 (numbering 0\&.\&.\&.n)\&. The missing node coordinates are calculated from the node coordinates of the linear tetrahedra and the lists px, py, pz' are extended correspondingly\&. 
.br

.PP
The property values are interpolated onto the newly generated points just as the node coordinates are\&. 
.br

.PP

.br
 \fBInput\fP \fBArguments\fP 

.PP
The supplied \fBVSet\fP must hold the "P-data" 'plist', 'pfverts' 'px', 'py', 'pz', in order to be processable\&. 
.br

.PP

.br
 \fBImplementation\fP 

.PP
The numbering of the new nodes starts from previous-nodes+1 and goes to new-total nodes of the mesh\&. This approach implies that, if node numbers are used to determine the placement in global solution matrices, nodes from a single triangle will be separated by many rows/cols in the global solution matrix\&. If a solver is used, which applies no pre-conditioning of the solution matrix, before inverting the solution matrix, this numbering leads to high storage requirements and long convergence times\&. In this case, an algorithm like the Cuthill-McKhee node-numbering graph-tree traversal should be used to improve the matrix occupancy and to reduce the number of nodes which are far off the diagonal\&. 
.br

.PP

.br
 \fBApplication\fP 

.PP

.br
 \fBMessages\fP 

.PP
tested: 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::VSetConverter\fP< dim >::ConvertLinearToBarycentricTriangles (\fBVSet\fP< dim > & vset)"

.PP
create a mesh of 7-noded barycentric triangular finite elements Takes the plist, px, py, pz etc\&. data from the \fBVSet<dim>\fP and changes the the linear triagular element to a 7-noded quadratic barycentric triangle according to the element specifications supplied by the barycentric 7-noded triangular finite element\&. 
.br

.PP
The Vset is modified according to the new specifications and the property values are interpolated onto the newly generated points just as the node coordinates are\&.

.PP
In the process the 'plist', 'px', 'py', 'pz', 'bflags' arrays in the Vdata are changed to adapt to the higher-order element\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The numbering of the new nodes starts from previous-nodes+1 and goes to new-total nodes of the mesh\&. This approach implies that, if node numbers are used to determine the placement in global solution matrices, nodes from a single triangle will be separated by many rows/cols in the global solution matrix\&. If a solver is used, which applies no pre-conditioning of the solution matrix, before inverting the solution matrix, this numbering leads to high storage requirements and long convergence times\&. In this case, an algorithm like the Cuthill-McKhee node-numbering graph-tree traversal should be used to improve the matrix occupancy and to reduce the number of nodes which are far off the diagonal\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::VSetConverter\fP< dim >::ConvertLinearToQuadraticTetrahedra (\fBVSet\fP< dim > & vset)"

.PP
create 10-noded tetrahedra from 4-noded ones void \fBVSetConverter<dim>::ConvertLinearToQuadraticTetrahedra( VSet<dim>& vset )\fP

.PP

.br
 \fBDescription\fP 

.PP
Interpolates midside node locations onto the sides of the quadratic tetrahedron and adds these points as nodes to the \fBVSet<dim>\fP which is returned\&. 
.br

.PP
The node numbering of the tetrahedron is: 
.PP
.nf
      ^ t
      |
      |

    4 o
      | \\
      |   \\
   10 o     o 9
      |      \\

.fi
.PP
 8 o | \\ 1 o -- o --- o 3 --> s / 7 / 
.br
 5 o o 6 / / o 2 
.br
 r 
.br

.PP

.br
 \fBInput\fP \fBArguments\fP 

.PP
A reference to the \fBVSet<dim>\fP which shall be modified by the function\&. 
.br

.PP

.br
 \fBOutput\fP \fBArguments\fP & Return Value

.PP
The modified \fBVSet<dim>\fP in returned into the first method argument\&. 
.br

.PP

.br
 \fBImplementation\fP 

.PP

.br
 \fBApplication\fP 

.PP
To facilitate computations with quadratic tetrahedral elements on the basis of simple tetrahedral element meshes\&. 
.br

.PP

.br
 \fBMessages\fP 

.PP
tested: O\&.K\&. SKM 4/3/02 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::VSetConverter\fP< dim >::ConvertLinearToQuadraticTriangles (\fBVSet\fP< dim > & vset)"

.PP
turn triangular element mesh data to target element data Takes the plist, px, py, pz etc\&. data from the \fBVSet<dim>\fP and changes the order of the interpolation functions of linear triangular elements to quadratic\&.

.PP
The Vset is modified according to the new specifications and the property values are interpolated onto the newly generated points just as the node coordinates are\&.

.PP
In the process the 'plist', 'px', 'py', 'pz', 'bflags' arrays in the Vdata are changed to adapt to the quadratic element\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvset\fP the initialized \fBVSet\fP with the data described above as needed to carry out the conversion\&. 
.br
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The numbering of the new nodes starts from previous-nodes+1 and goes to new-total nodes of the mesh\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
This approach implies that, if node numbers are used to determine the placement in global solution matrices, nodes from a single triangle will be separated by many rows/cols in the global solution matrix\&. If a solver is used, which applies no pre-conditioning of the solution matrix, before inverting the solution matrix, this numbering leads to high storage requirements and long convergence times\&. In this case, an algorithm like the Cuthill-McKhee node-numbering graph-tree traversal should be used to improve the matrix occupancy and to reduce the number of nodes which are far off the diagonal\&. 
.RE
.PP

